{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b4ffd85a64964d8f","name":"card_unit_tsu_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/CovertOp/units/card_unit_tsu_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"TSU REGIMENT","text":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDestruction: Destroy the unit targeted.","flavorText":"The Tsu Regiment, formally known as the 133rd Infantry regiment, was a unit of the 116th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army. The division was formed in May 1938. In June that year it was transferred to Shanghai, and then to the Dabie Mountains in China where it participated in the Battle of Wuhan against the Chinese forces. Between 1939 and 1944 the division participated in various battles and campaigns in China, including the Battle of Changde and the Battle of Changsha. In October 1944 the 133rd Division was transferred to the Twentieth Army to take part in the Battle of Hengyang as part of Operation Ichi-Go. After intense fighting the division suffered heavy losses, but the battle ended with the Japanese capture of the city. In 1945 the division participated in the Battle of West Henan–North Hubei, a Japanese victory. The division was stationed in the city of Hengyang when Japan surrendered on August 15th, 1945.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":5,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_tsu_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_tsu_regiment_title","SourceString":"TSU REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"TSU REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":5,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_tsu_regiment_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDestruction: Destroy the unit targeted.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Target a unit. \r\nDestruction: Destroy the unit targeted."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_tsu_regiment_history","SourceString":"The Tsu Regiment, formally known as the 133rd Infantry regiment, was a unit of the 116th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army. The division was formed in May 1938. In June that year it was transferred to Shanghai, and then to the Dabie Mountains in China where it participated in the Battle of Wuhan against the Chinese forces. Between 1939 and 1944 the division participated in various battles and campaigns in China, including the Battle of Changde and the Battle of Changsha. In October 1944 the 133rd Division was transferred to the Twentieth Army to take part in the Battle of Hengyang as part of Operation Ichi-Go. After intense fighting the division suffered heavy losses, but the battle ended with the Japanese capture of the city. In 1945 the division participated in the Battle of West Henan–North Hubei, a Japanese victory. The division was stationed in the city of Hengyang when Japan surrendered on August 15th, 1945.","LocalizedString":"The Tsu Regiment, formally known as the 133rd Infantry regiment, was a unit of the 116th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army. The division was formed in May 1938. In June that year it was transferred to Shanghai, and then to the Dabie Mountains in China where it participated in the Battle of Wuhan against the Chinese forces. Between 1939 and 1944 the division participated in various battles and campaigns in China, including the Battle of Changde and the Battle of Changsha. In October 1944 the 133rd Division was transferred to the Twentieth Army to take part in the Battle of Hengyang as part of Operation Ichi-Go. After intense fighting the division suffered heavy losses, but the battle ended with the Japanese capture of the city. In 1945 the division participated in the Battle of West Henan–North Hubei, a Japanese victory. The division was stationed in the city of Hengyang when Japan surrendered on August 15th, 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,